WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.636
Dorothy lived on a farm in Kansas with her aunt Em and uncle Henry.

2
00:00:06.637 --> 00:00:09.973
Her aunt and uncle were hardworking and quiet.

3
00:00:09.974 --> 00:00:14.357
They spent all their time working, so they had no time to play with Dorothy.

4
00:00:14.358 --> 00:00:19.287
Dorothy would have been lonely if it weren't for her dog, Toto.

5
00:00:19.288 --> 00:00:25.008
One day Dorothy and Toto stopped playing, and Aunt Em and Uncle Henry stopped working.

6
00:00:25.009 --> 00:00:30.003
They all looked at the sky. Dorothy didn't like what she saw.

7
00:00:30.004 --> 00:00:33.560
Across the field the sky was the color of night.

8
00:00:33.561 --> 00:00:40.589
Suddenly a flash of lightning split the darkness, and the wind began to howl.

9
00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:44.078
"A cyclone is coming," said Uncle Henry.

10
00:00:44.079 --> 00:00:49.278
"I'll help the animals. Em, you and Dorothy go to the storm cellar."

11
00:00:49.279 --> 00:00:54.468
Toto jumped out of Dorothy's arms, ran into the house, and hid under a bed.

12
00:00:54.469 --> 00:00:58.822
Aunt Em ran to the storm cellar, but Dorothy ran after Toto.

13
00:00:58.823 --> 00:01:05.247
The house shook violently and then began to spin.

14
00:01:05.248 --> 00:01:08.773
The house shook again, and the spinning stopped.

15
00:01:08.774 --> 00:01:13.144
Holding Toto in her arms, Dorothy looked out the window.

16
00:01:13.145 --> 00:01:16.090
She was amazed by what she saw.

17
00:01:16.091 --> 00:01:25.584
The boring, colorless landscape of Kansas had been replaced with flowers, fountains, and brightly colored birds.

18
00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:30.888
Strange, tiny people were running toward the house.

19
00:01:30.889 --> 00:01:34.605
Outside, an old woman approached Dorothy and bowed.

20
00:01:34.606 --> 00:01:38.464
"You're a great hero," said the woman.

21
00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:41.799
"We thank you for killing the Wicked Witch of the East.

22
00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:43.936
The Munchkins are free!"

23
00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:48.081
The other people cheered, but Dorothy was confused.

24
00:01:48.082 --> 00:01:53.385
"I haven't killed anyone," she said fearfully.

25
00:01:53.386 --> 00:01:57.238
"Well, your house did," said the old woman.

26
00:01:57.239 --> 00:02:01.265
"And the result is the same—the Munchkins are free."

27
00:02:01.266 --> 00:02:07.660
"Oh dear!" cried Dorothy. "The house fell on her. Who was she?"

28
00:02:07.661 --> 00:02:12.031
"She was the Wicked Witch of the East," said the woman.

29
00:02:12.032 --> 00:02:15.498
"And the Munchkins were her slaves."

30
00:02:15.499 --> 00:02:19.326
"Are you a Munchkin?" asked Dorothy.

31
00:02:19.327 --> 00:02:23.844
"Oh, no. I am the Good Witch of the North.

32
00:02:23.845 --> 00:02:27.695
I came because I heard the Wicked Witch was dead."

33
00:02:27.696 --> 00:02:32.827
"Where I come from," said Dorothy, "all witches are dead."

34
00:02:32.828 --> 00:02:36.555
"That doesn't surprise me," said the Good Witch.

35
00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:43.623
"If houses often fall from the sky, not even the Great Oz could survive."

36
00:02:43.624 --> 00:02:47.386
"The Great Oz?" asked Dorothy.

37
00:02:47.387 --> 00:02:51.342
"Yes, the Wizard of Oz," answered the Good Witch.

38
00:02:51.343 --> 00:02:55.701
"He is the most powerful wizard in the land."

39
00:02:55.702 --> 00:03:01.832
Dorothy was about to ask something when the Munchkins all gave a sudden shout.

40
00:03:01.833 --> 00:03:07.994
The body of the Wicked Witch was gone. Only her silver shoes were left.

41
00:03:07.995 --> 00:03:12.270
"These shoes are yours now," said the Good Witch.

42
00:03:12.271 --> 00:03:17.287
"They are magical, but I do not know what they do."

43
00:03:17.288 --> 00:03:20.800
"Can they take me back to Kansas?" said Dorothy.

44
00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:27.179
"Maybe," said the Good Witch, "but you should ask the Wizard of Oz."

45
00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:30.782
"Where does he live?" asked Dorothy.

46
00:03:30.783 --> 00:03:35.009
"He lives in the Emerald City," said the Good Witch.

47
00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:40.808
"It's a long journey, but easy if you follow the Yellow Brick Road."

48
00:03:40.809 --> 00:03:44.522
"The Yellow Brick Road?" said Dorothy.

49
00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:47.795
"Yes," answered the Good Witch.

50
00:03:47.796 --> 00:03:54.179
"It begins over there and goes right to the Emerald City."

51
00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:57.996
"Will you come with me?" asked Dorothy hopefully.

52
00:03:57.997 --> 00:04:03.757
"No, I cannot," said the Good Witch. "But I will give you a kiss.

53
00:04:03.758 --> 00:04:08.793
My kiss will protect you. No one will harm you.

54
00:04:08.794 --> 00:04:15.046
Well, no one except maybe the Wicked Witch of the West."

55
00:04:15.047 --> 00:04:19.289
"The Wicked Witch of the West?" said Dorothy, puzzled.

56
00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:24.754
"Yes, you must be careful of her," said the Good Witch.

57
00:04:24.755 --> 00:04:30.015
Dorothy had many questions, but the Good Witch kissed her on the forehead just then.

58
00:04:30.016 --> 00:04:35.009
Dorothy could feel the magic enveloping her body.

59
00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:42.488
"Good-bye, good luck, and remember: stay on the Yellow Brick Road," said the Good Witch.

60
00:04:42.489 --> 00:04:49.580
Toto gave a loud bark as the Good Witch suddenly disappeared.

61
00:04:49.581 --> 00:04:56.007
"Well, Toto," said Dorothy, "I guess we should pack and then follow the Yellow Brick Road."

62
00:04:56.008 --> 00:05:01.698
She put some food in her picnic basket and then locked the door to her house.

63
00:05:01.699 --> 00:05:09.586
"Come along, Toto. It's time to go see the Wizard."

